# Design System Authoring

## Component API Design

- Every component must accept a `className` prop for consumer-side overrides via `tailwind-merge`.
- Use a `variants` pattern for visual variations — pass variant names as props, not raw classes.
- Keep prop interfaces minimal — prefer composition over configuration.

```tsx
// ✅ Composable, accepts className, uses variants
interface ButtonProps {
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'ghost' | 'danger';
  size?: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg';
  children: React.ReactNode;
  className?: string;
  // ...rest HTML button props via ComponentPropsWithoutRef
}
```

## Accessibility (a11y)

- All interactive components must be keyboard navigable.
- Use semantic HTML elements (`button`, `nav`, `table`, `th`, `td`) — not divs with click handlers.
- Include `aria-label` on icon-only buttons and non-text interactive elements.
- Use Radix UI or React Aria primitives for complex widgets (modals, dropdowns, tooltips).
- Color alone must never convey meaning — pair with icons or text (e.g., injury status).

## Composition Over Props

- Prefer children/slots over deeply nested prop objects.
- Build complex components by composing primitives.

```tsx
// ✅ Composable
<Card>
  <Card.Header>
    <PlayerAvatar src={player.photo} />
    <Badge variant="position">{player.position}</Badge>
  </Card.Header>
  <Card.Body>{/* stats */}</Card.Body>
</Card>

// ❌ Monolithic prop bag
<Card header={...} body={...} avatar={...} badge={...} />
```

## File & Export Rules

- One component per file.
- Named exports only — no default exports.
- Every component directory must have an `index.ts` barrel re-exporting its public API.
- The top-level `design-system/index.ts` re-exports everything consumers need.

## Statefulness

- Design system components are **stateless/controlled** by default.
- Internal state is acceptable only for UI concerns (open/closed, hover, focus).
- Data, selection state, and form values are always controlled via props.

## Client Component Directive

- Most design system components will be **Client Components** because they use interactivity (`useState`, `onClick`, etc.).
- Add `'use client'` at the top of each component file that needs it.
- Pure display-only components (e.g., a `Badge` that just renders text with styling) can remain Server Components — do NOT add `'use client'` unless the component actually uses client-side APIs.
- The barrel `index.ts` does NOT need `'use client'` — it only re-exports.
